Chapter: QuoteFromStore

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  quotes "sha256:71f85b21050759c45724ab3a7eebe9eb36453b16b5c3878c6fdea78732bce71b" as Sorted
  trusting "fcfbf1f0f3f0f3ff" "30a23f41fc17ec2aac012d0755750484a535afbcff80882094d569bbc7bdefff" 10000
  trusting above 5000

 The same quotation codex/test/quotes-gate.codex proves through the
 offered-works blob, proven here through the fact store instead. There is
 no %%QUOTED-WORKS%% section: the work is not beside the source. It is a
 signed, content-addressed fact on the disk this source is compiled
 against, written there by codex/test/apps/store-quoted-work. The compiler
 reads the store, finds the work by the digest quoted above, checks it
 through the same four guards, and only then is sort-ascending a name this
 chapter may use. This is the founding document's "delete GitHub" reduced
 to one program: the source of a quotation lives in the repository, not in
 a file handed alongside.

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("sorted=" & show (sort-ascending 5))
  end

